# constraints: for base b with removal set R (bits set) and add-set A observed: all observed adds and some removals are in top 5.
# If |A| + |R| >= 5: list is exactly 5 neighbors: the observed adds A plus (5-|A|) removals. Unobserved adds U are after ALL of the included ones. We don't know which removals are included.
# So constraints: for a in A, u in U: a < u.  Also if 5-|A| < |R| then some removals are excluded... 
# Let's collect a < u constraints and check acyclicity, build order.
import collections
edges=collections.defaultdict(set)
nodes=set(range(256))
